From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pi-hrx-fabric <fabric@1bit.local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:22:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] accel/amdxdna: check the power-cycle throttle before
 touching any context

0004 stops a throttled power-cycle (-EBUSY from aie2_hw_reset() inside the rate-limit window) from being
counted as the reset's failure, but the recovery still runs both context walks: every context is stopped
and then restarted against an array that was NOT power-cycled. A restart that fails for that reason sets
rarg.failed, and rarg.failed latches hw_dead - so "any two TDRs inside 60 s take the array" stays
reachable through the other latch.

Check the throttle first, under the dev_lock the recovery already holds, and return having touched
nothing: no context stopped, no restart attempted, no hw_dead. Pending jobs stay pending and the next
watchdog tick (tdr_timeout_ms=15000) retries once the window has passed. The -EBUSY handling in 0004 stays
as belt-and-braces with a comment, since with dev_lock held for the whole pass it is not reachable.

This is patch 0009 on strixhalo (2026-11-04). Verified: adding it to pin + 0001 + 0002 + 0004 leaves every
.c/.h byte-identical to the sources the shipping build came from, and rebuilds to
srcversion BBE1E5F0EE7A5FB235CA811 - the 0007+0008+0009 module.

Signed-off-by: bong-water-water-bong <bong-water-water-bong@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c
@@ -143,6 +143,20 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * aie2_tdr_recovery_throttled - is a power-cycle still inside the rate-limit window?
+ *
+ * aie2_hw_reset() refuses a second power-cycle within AIE2_HW_RESET_MIN_INTERVAL_MS with -EBUSY. That is "not yet",
+ * so the recovery must not be attempted at all: the array has not been power-cycled, which means every context would be
+ * stopped and restarted against a still-wedged device - and a restart that fails for that reason sets rarg->failed,
+ * which latches hw_dead. Same predicate as aie2_hw_reset() so the two cannot disagree.
+ */
+static bool aie2_tdr_recovery_throttled(struct amdxdna_dev_hdl *ndev)
+{
+	return time_before(jiffies,
+			   ndev->last_reset_jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(AIE2_HW_RESET_MIN_INTERVAL_MS));
+}
+
 static void aie2_tdr_recover_all(struct amdxdna_dev *xdna)
 {
 	struct amdxdna_dev_hdl *ndev = xdna->dev_handle;
@@ -151,6 +165,14 @@
 	bool fw_dead = false;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (aie2_tdr_recovery_throttled(ndev)) {
+		XDNA_WARN(xdna,
+			  "TDR recovery throttled: last power-cycle %u ms ago (< %d ms), retrying on the next watchdog tick; no context touched",
+			  jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - ndev->last_reset_jiffies),
+			  AIE2_HW_RESET_MIN_INTERVAL_MS);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	amdxdna_for_each_client(xdna, client)
 		amdxdna_hwctx_walk(client, &fw_dead, NULL, aie2_tdr_stop_hwctx);
 
